{% extends "base_app.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Contribute & invite friends — GamerAI{% endblock %}
{% block extra_css %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/contribute.css">
{% endblock %}

{% block topbar_actions %}
    {% if me %}
    <a href="/" class="hide-mobile">← chat</a>
    <a href="/account">{{ me.username or me.email or 'account' }}</a>
    <a href="/logout">sign out</a>
    {% else %}
    <a href="/login">sign in</a>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="page">

  <section class="hero">
    <h1>An AI suite powered by your friends and neighbors</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      GamerAI runs on contributors' gaming PCs. You run a small agent
      when your machine is idle; in return, you and the people you
      invite get free access to the whole toolbox — chat, image
      generation, and more — without a subscription and without
      anyone harvesting your prompts to train their model.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>How it works, honestly</h2>
    <ol class="how">
      <li>
        <strong>You run the agent on your gaming PC.</strong> It picks
        up jobs from the shared queue only when the machine is idle
        — gaming or working takes priority. Power scales with demand,
        not uptime: near-zero when nothing's running, full GPU draw
        only during active inference.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You earn tier-based access</strong> based on uptime,
        capability, and how many jobs you actually serve. Each tier
        raises the daily quota for you and the friends you invite.
        No subscription, no billing — your contribution <em>is</em>
        the membership.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You invite the people you want on the network.</strong>
        Each invite is a link you share over your own channel (text,
        Slack, however) — we don't run an email service. Your
        invitees use the suite under your tier's quota; you can
        adjust their daily cap or revoke their access from your
        Account page anytime.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>How we keep the lights on</h2>
    <p>
      When the contributor pool has spare capacity, we offer it to
      outside customers and use that revenue to keep the coordinator
      running. The majority of what comes in flows back to the
      contributors whose machines did the work; the rest covers
      operating costs. The platform never charges you and never sells
      your prompts.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Set up on Windows in five minutes</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Windows only for now.
    </p>

    <h3>What you need</h3>
    <ul class="reqs">
      <li><strong>Windows 10 or 11</strong> on a desktop or laptop
        with a discrete GPU.</li>
      <li><strong>NVIDIA GPU with ≥6 GB VRAM</strong> for the chat
        tool. 8+ GB unlocks image generation as well.</li>
      <li><strong>A recent driver</strong> (Studio or Game Ready,
        either is fine).</li>
      <li><strong>A GamerAI account</strong> — accept an invite from
        someone already on the network, or
        <a href="/login">sign in</a> if you already have one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Install</h3>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        Download the installer:
        <a class="btn" href="/download/GamerAI-Agent-Setup.exe">
          GamerAI-Agent-Setup.exe
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Run it. <strong>Windows SmartScreen</strong> will show a
        "Windows protected your PC" warning the first time — the
        binary isn't code-signed yet. Click <em>More info</em> →
        <em>Run anyway</em>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open the agent from the Start menu. The first run prints a
        pairing URL and opens your default browser to it.
      </li>
      <li>
        On the browser page, click <em>Pair this PC</em>. You'll
        need to be signed in — if you're not, sign in first and the
        page will bounce back. The agent picks up its credentials
        automatically.
      </li>
      <li>
        Leave the agent running. It autostarts at login and only
        serves jobs while your machine is idle.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="hint">
      Already paired? Open your <a href="/account">Account page</a>
      to see your tier and the friends you've invited.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>
{% endblock %}
